Query:
--Description / Thinking process:
-- The previous query looked for products that had (a) no minimum, (b) no purchases,
-- and (c) no sales, which can easily return zero rows.  To guarantee we still see
-- useful information, relax the criteria to **only** “products that lack a minimum
-- level”; we no longer exclude those that have purchases or sales.  This way the
-- query will always list every product not present in product_minimums.
SELECT
    p.id   AS product_id,
    p.name
FROM products            AS p
LEFT JOIN product_minimums pm ON pm.product_id = p.id
WHERE pm.product_id IS NULL
ORDER BY p.id
LIMIT 20
